# Laravel Pulse Development

## Documentation

Use ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___search-docs___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ for detailed Laravel Pulse patterns and documentation, including card layout customization, user resolver configuration, all recorder options, sampling, dedicated database connections, Vite/CSS integration, Tailwind scoping, blade card components, and lazy loading.

## Installation

Pulse stores data in your application's database. The current package supports MySQL, MariaDB, PostgreSQL, and SQLite.

___SINGLE_BACKTICK______SINGLE_BACKTICK______SINGLE_BACKTICK___bash
composer require laravel/pulse
<?php echo e($assist->artisanCommand('vendor:publish --provider="Laravel\Pulse\PulseServiceProvider"')); ?>

<?php echo e($assist->artisanCommand('migrate')); ?>

___SINGLE_BACKTICK______SINGLE_BACKTICK______SINGLE_BACKTICK___

The dashboard is available at ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___/pulse___SINGLE_BACKTICK___. 

## Dashboard Authorization

Define the ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___viewPulse___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ gate in ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___AppServiceProvider::boot()___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ to enable production access:

___BOOST_SNIPPET_0___

Without this gate, the dashboard is inaccessible in all non-local environments.

