The ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___Servers___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ recorder requires ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___pulse:check___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ running as a persistent daemon (Supervisor recommended).

### Filtering Entries

Use ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___Pulse::filter()___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ in ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___AppServiceProvider::boot()___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ to exclude entries globally. Return ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___true___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ to record, ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___false___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ to skip:

___BOOST_SNIPPET_2___

## Performance

### Redis Ingest

Offload entry writes from the request cycle to a Redis stream (requires Redis 6.2+ and ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___phpredis___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ or ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___predis___SINGLE_BACKTICK___):

___SINGLE_BACKTICK______SINGLE_BACKTICK______SINGLE_BACKTICK___ini
PULSE_INGEST_DRIVER=redis
PULSE_REDIS_CONNECTION=pulse
___SINGLE_BACKTICK______SINGLE_BACKTICK______SINGLE_BACKTICK___

Run a worker to drain the Redis stream into the database:

___SINGLE_BACKTICK______SINGLE_BACKTICK______SINGLE_BACKTICK___bash
<?php echo e($assist->artisanCommand('pulse:work')); ?>

___SINGLE_BACKTICK______SINGLE_BACKTICK______SINGLE_BACKTICK___

Signal a graceful restart during deployment (requires a working cache driver):

___SINGLE_BACKTICK______SINGLE_BACKTICK______SINGLE_BACKTICK___bash
<?php echo e($assist->artisanCommand('pulse:restart')); ?>

___SINGLE_BACKTICK______SINGLE_BACKTICK______SINGLE_BACKTICK___

## Custom Cards

Custom cards are Livewire components extending Pulse's base ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___Card___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ class.

### Recording Entries

Call ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___Pulse::record()___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ from a recorder, listener, or observer. Chain aggregation methods (___SINGLE_BACKTICK___avg___SINGLE_BACKTICK___, ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___count___SINGLE_BACKTICK___, ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___max___SINGLE_BACKTICK___, ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___min___SINGLE_BACKTICK___, ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___sum___SINGLE_BACKTICK___) in a single call:

___BOOST_SNIPPET_3___

When the entry is tied to the authenticated user, use ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___Pulse::resolveAuthenticatedUserId()___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ instead of ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___Auth::id()___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ to respect custom user resolvers.

### Card Component

___BOOST_SNIPPET_4___

___SINGLE_BACKTICK___$this->aggregate(type, aggregates)___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ returns a ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___Collection___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ of ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___stdClass___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ objects with ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___key___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ and one property per aggregation method. ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___$this->aggregateTotal(type, aggregate)___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ returns a single scalar.

### Custom Recorders

A recorder is a plain class with a ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___$listen___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ array of Laravel events:

